%N A399170 Triangle read by rows: T(n,k) is the number of rooted binary unlabeled general galled trees with n leaves and exactly k galls, 0 <= k <= n-1.
%C A399170 For fixed k, the asymptotic growth of T(n,k) with increasing n follows T(n,k) ~ (2^(2*k-1) / ((2*k)!*g^(4*k-1)*sqrt(Pi))) * n^(2*k - 3/2) * r^(-n), where g=1.13003... and r=0.40270... (eq. 16 of Agranat-Tamir et al., Adv. Appl. Math. 180 (2026), 103131).
%H A399170 Lily Agranat-Tamir, Michael Fuchs, Bernhard Gittenberger, Noah A. Rosenberg, and Karthik V. Seetharaman, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.aam.2026.103131">Combinatorial comparison of general galled trees, time-consistent galled trees, and simplex time-consistent galled trees</a>, Adv. Appl. Math. 180, 103131 (2026). See Table 1.
%F A399170 G.f. satisfies A(x,y) = x + (1/2)*A(x,y)^2 + (1/2)*A(x^2,y^2) + (1/2)*y*A(x,y)*( (A(x,y)/(1-A(x,y)))^2 + A(x^2,y^2)/(1-A(x^2,y^2)) ) + y*A(x,y)^2/(1-A(x,y)) (eq. 11 of Agranat-Tamir et al. (2026)).
%e A399170 Triangle begins:
